"                     int <replaceable>recurInterval</replaceable>, \n"
"                     const QString&amp; <replaceable>endDateTime</"
"replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3329 index.docbook:3924
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>message</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the text of the message to be scheduled, or if <parameter>flags</"
"parameter> has the <userinput>DISPLAY_COMMAND</userinput> bit set, specifies "
"the command line to execute to generate the message text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3339 index.docbook:3558 index.docbook:3750 index.docbook:3939
#, no-c-format
msgid "dateTime"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3341 index.docbook:3560 index.docbook:3752 index.docbook:3941
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the scheduled date, or date and time, at which the message should "
"be displayed. For a date-only alarm, the string should be in the format "
"<replaceable>YYYY-MM-DD [TZ]</replaceable> (as returned by "
"<methodname>QDate::toString(Qt::ISODate)</methodname>). For an alarm with a "
"date and time, the string should be in the format <replaceable>YYYY-MM-DDTHH:"
"MM[:SS] [TZ]</replaceable> (as returned by <methodname>QDateTime::toString"
"(Qt::ISODate)</methodname>) or <replaceable>HH:MM[:SS] [Clock]</replaceable> "
"(as returned by <methodname>QTime::toString(Qt::ISODate)</methodname>). If "
"no date is specified, today's date is used. Note that any seconds value is "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3353 index.docbook:3572 index.docbook:3764 index.docbook:3953
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If no time zone is specified, the local system time zone is assumed. If a "
"time zone specifier <replaceable>TZ</replaceable> is present, it may be the "
"name of a system time zone (&eg; <userinput>Europe/London</userinput>), "
"<userinput>UTC</userinput> representing the UTC time zone, or "
"<userinput>Clock</userinput> to use the local computer clock and ignore time "
"zones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3363 index.docbook:3582 index.docbook:3774 index.docbook:3963
#, no-c-format
msgid "lateCancel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3365 index.docbook:3584 index.docbook:3776 index.docbook:3965
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes the alarm to be canceled if it cannot be triggered within the "
"specified number of minutes after the alarm's scheduled time. If the value "
"is 0, the alarm will not be canceled no matter how late it is triggered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3373 index.docbook:3592 index.docbook:3784 index.docbook:3973
#, no-c-format
msgid "flags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3375
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the logical OR of the desired alarm flags. The flag bits are those "
"defined in class <classname>KAlarmIface</classname> in <filename>kalarmiface."
"h</filename>. Note that not all flag bits are applicable to message alarms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3383 index.docbook:3602
#, no-c-format
msgid "bgColor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3385
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the background color for displaying the message. The string may be "
"in the format <quote>#RRGGBB</quote> (as returned by <methodname>QColor::name"
"()</methodname>) where RR, GG and BB are two-digit hexadecimal values for "
"red, green and blue. Alternatively the string may be in any of the other "
"formats accepted by <methodname>QColor::setNamedColor()</methodname>, such "
"as a name from the X color database (&eg; <quote>red</quote> or "
"<quote>steelblue</quote>). Set the string to null to specify the current "
"default background color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3398
#, no-c-format
msgid "fgColor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the foreground color for displaying the message. The format of the "
"string is the same as for <parameter>bgColor</parameter>, or alternatively "
"set the string to null to specify the current default foreground color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3408
#, no-c-format
msgid "font"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3410
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the font for displaying the message. The format of the string is "
"that output by <methodname>QFont::toString()</methodname>. Set the string to "
"null to use the default message font current at the time the message is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3418 index.docbook:3617
#, no-c-format
msgid "audioURL"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3420 index.docbook:3619
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the audio file which is to be played when the message is "
"displayed. Set the value to null if no audio file is to be played."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3427 index.docbook:3626
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>reminder</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3429 index.docbook:3628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of minutes in advance of the main alarm and of each of "
"its recurrences (if any) at which a reminder alarm should be displayed. "
"Specify 0 if no reminder is required."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3436 index.docbook:3635 index.docbook:3794 index.docbook:3983
#, no-c-format
msgid "recurrence"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3438 index.docbook:3637 index.docbook:3796 index.docbook:3985
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies a regular recurrence for the alarm, using iCalendar syntax as "
"defined in <ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/rfc2445.html"
"\">RFC2445</ulink>. For example, <quote>FREQ=MONTHLY;COUNT=4;INTERVAL=3;"
"BYDAY=-1MO</quote> would specify 4 repetitions at 3-monthly intervals on the "
"last Monday of the month. For a non-recurring alarm, specify an empty string."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3449 index.docbook:3648 index.docbook:3807 index.docbook:3996
#, no-c-format
msgid "recurType"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3451 index.docbook:3650 index.docbook:3809 index.docbook:3998
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the recurrence type for the alarm. The permissible values are "
"MINUTELY, DAILY, WEEKLY, MONTHLY, YEARLY. These are defined in class "
"<classname>KAlarmIface</classname> in <filename>kalarmiface.h</filename>. "
"Monthly recurrences are of the day of the month type, and yearly recurrences "
"are of the date in the year type, with the date in both cases taken from the "
"<parameter>dateTime</parameter> parameter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3462 index.docbook:3661 index.docbook:3820 index.docbook:4009
#, no-c-format
msgid "recurInterval"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3464 index.docbook:3663 index.docbook:3822 index.docbook:4011
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of periods (minutes/days/weeks/months/years as "
"specified by <parameter>recurType</parameter>) between recurrences of the "
"alarm."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3472 index.docbook:3671 index.docbook:3830 index.docbook:4019
#, no-c-format
msgid "recurCount"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3474 index.docbook:3673 index.docbook:3832 index.docbook:4021
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of times that the alarm should be repeated. Specify -1 "
"to repeat the alarm indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3480 index.docbook:3679 index.docbook:3838 index.docbook:4027
#, no-c-format
msgid "endDateTime"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3482 index.docbook:3681 index.docbook:3840 index.docbook:4029
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the end date, or date and time, for recurrences of the alarm. If "
"<parameter>dateTime</parameter> includes a time, this parameter must also "
"include a time; if <parameter>dateTime</parameter> contains only a date, "
"this parameter must also contain only a date. It must not contain a time "
"zone specifier; the same time zone as for <parameter>dateTime</parameter> is "
"used to interpret this parameter's value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3493 index.docbook:3692 index.docbook:3851 index.docbook:4040
#, no-c-format
msgid "subRepeatInterval"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3495 index.docbook:3694 index.docbook:3853 index.docbook:4042
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of minutes between sub-repetitions of the alarm. "
"Specify 0 for no sub-repetition. Ignored if no recurrence is specified."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3502 index.docbook:3701 index.docbook:3860 index.docbook:4049
#, no-c-format
msgid "subRepeatCount"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3504 index.docbook:3703 index.docbook:3862 index.docbook:4051
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of sub-repetitions of the alarm, including the initial "
"occurrence."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3514
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>scheduleMessage()</function> is a &DCOP; call to schedule the "
"specified alarm message for display at the specified date and time. It has "
"three forms. The most general form allows an arbitrary recurrence to be "
"specified &ndash; use this also for non-repeating alarms. The other forms "
"provide convenient access to a restricted set of alarm recurrence types, one "
"specifying a repetition count and the other an end time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3522
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the scheduled time (including any repetitions) has already passed, "
"&kalarm; immediately displays the message (unless the <parameter>lateCancel</"
"parameter> value indicates that it is now too late to display the alarm, in "
"which case &kalarm; ignores the request). If the scheduled time (or a "
"repetition) is in the future, &kalarm; adds the alarm message to the default "
"active alarm resource for later display."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refentrytitle
#: index.docbook:3534
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refentrytitle>scheduleFile</refentrytitle>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refname
#: index.docbook:3537
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refname>scheduleFile</refname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refpurpose
#: index.docbook:3538
#, no-c-format
msgid "schedule a new alarm which displays the contents of a text or image file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:3542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"bool scheduleFile(const KURL&amp; <replaceable>URL</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>dateTime</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>lateCancel</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>flags</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>bgColor</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const KURL&amp; <replaceable>audioURL</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>reminder</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>recurrence</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>subRepeatInterval</replaceable>, \n"
"                  int <replaceable>subRepeatCount</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:3543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"bool scheduleFile(const KURL&amp; <replaceable>URL</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>dateTime</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>lateCancel</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>flags</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>bgColor</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const KURL&amp; <replaceable>audioURL</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>reminder</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>recurType</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>recurInterval</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>recurCount</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:3544
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"bool scheduleFile(const KURL&amp; <replaceable>URL</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>dateTime</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>lateCancel</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>flags</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>bgColor</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const KURL&amp; <replaceable>audioURL</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>reminder</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>recurType</replaceable>,\n"
"                  int <replaceable>recurInterval</replaceable>,\n"
"                  const QString&amp; <replaceable>endDateTime</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3550
#, no-c-format
msgid "<parameter>URL</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the text or image file whose contents are to be displayed in the "
"message to be scheduled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the logical OR of the desired alarm flags. The flag bits are those "
"defined in class <classname>KAlarmIface</classname> in <filename>kalarmiface."
"h</filename>. Note that not all flag bits are applicable to file alarms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3604
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the background color for displaying the file. The string may be in "
"the format <quote>#RRGGBB</quote> (as returned by <methodname>QColor::name()"
"</methodname>) where RR, GG and BB are two-digit hexadecimal values for red, "
"green and blue. Alternatively the string may be in any of the other formats "
"accepted by <methodname>QColor::setNamedColor()</methodname>, such as a name "
"from the X color database (&eg; <quote>red</quote> or <quote>steelblue</"
"quote>). Set the string to null to specify the current default background "
"color."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3713
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>scheduleFile()</function> is a &DCOP; call to schedule the "
"specified text or image file for display at the specified date and time. "
"Apart from specifying a file path or &URL; and omitting the foreground color "
"and font, its usage is identical to <link linkend=\"scheduleMessage-descrip"
"\"><function>scheduleMessage</function></link> - see the description of that "
"function for further details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refentrytitle
#: index.docbook:3725
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refentrytitle>scheduleCommand</refentrytitle>"
msgstr ""

