"                   int <replaceable>recurInterval</replaceable>,\n"
"                   const QString&amp; <replaceable>endTime</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3900
#, no-c-format
msgid "fromID"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3902
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kmail; identity to use as the sender of the email. If empty, the "
"sender's email address will be that configured in &kalarm;'s <link linkend="
"\"preferences-email\">Email preferences</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3910
#, no-c-format
msgid "addresses"
msgstr "adreças"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3912
#, no-c-format
msgid "A comma separated list of recipients' email addresses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3917
#, no-c-format
msgid "subject"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3919
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specifies the subject line of the email."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3926
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specifies the email message body."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:3931
#, no-c-format
msgid "attachments"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3933
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A comma-separated list of paths or &URL;s of files to send as email "
"attachments."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:3975
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the logical OR of the desired alarm flags. The flag bits are those "
"defined in class <classname>KAlarmIface</classname> in <filename>kalarmiface."
"h</filename>. Note that not all flag bits are applicable to email alarms."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4061
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>scheduleEmail()</function> is a &DCOP; call to schedule the "
"specified email for sending at the specified date and time. Apart from "
"specifying the email header and contents and omitting the message color, "
"font and audio file parameters, its usage is identical to <link linkend="
"\"scheduleMessage-descrip\"><function>scheduleMessage</function></link> - "
"see the description of that function for further details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refentrytitle
#: index.docbook:4073
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refentrytitle>edit</refentrytitle>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refname
#: index.docbook:4076
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refname>edit</refname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refpurpose
#: index.docbook:4077
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Display the <link linkend=\"alarm-edit-dlg\">Alarm Edit dialog</link> to "
"edit an alarm."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:4081
#, no-c-format
msgid "bool edit(const QString&amp; <replaceable>eventID</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4089
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specifies the unique ID of the event to be edited."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4096 index.docbook:4150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Return value"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4097
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<returnvalue>false</returnvalue> if the specified alarm could not be found "
"or is read-only, <returnvalue>true</returnvalue> otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>edit()</function> is a &DCOP; call to display the <link linkend="
"\"alarm-edit-dlg\">Alarm Edit dialog</link> to edit the specified alarm."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refentrytitle
#: index.docbook:4115
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refentrytitle>editNew</refentrytitle>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refname
#: index.docbook:4118
#, no-c-format
msgid "<refname>editNew</refname>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: refpurpose
#: index.docbook:4119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Display the <link linkend=\"alarm-edit-dlg\">Alarm Edit dialog</link> to "
"edit a new alarm."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:4123
#, no-c-format
msgid "bool editNew(int <replaceable>type</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: synopsis
#: index.docbook:4124
#, no-c-format
msgid "bool editNew(const QString&amp; <replaceable>templateName</replaceable>)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:4130
#, no-c-format
msgid "type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Specifies the alarm type. The permissible values are DISPLAY, COMMAND, "
"EMAIL. These are defined in class <classname>KAlarmIface</classname> in "
"<filename>kalarmiface.h</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: parameter
#: index.docbook:4140
#, no-c-format
msgid "templateName"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specifies the name of an alarm template to base the new alarm on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<returnvalue>false</returnvalue> if <parameter>type</parameter> has an "
"invalid value, or if no template with the name <parameter>templateName</"
"parameter> can be found; <returnvalue>true</returnvalue> otherwise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<function>editNew()</function> is a &DCOP; call to display the <link linkend="
"\"alarm-edit-dlg\">Alarm Edit dialog</link> to edit a new alarm. If an alarm "
"type is specified as a parameter, a blank dialog is displayed. "
"Alternatively, if an alarm template name is specified as a parameter, the "
"dialog is preset with details from the template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4173
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Interface"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4175
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Command line options are provided to enable other programs (such as the "
"<application>alarm daemon</application>) to start up &kalarm; if it is not "
"already running, in order to trigger or cancel scheduled alarms, or schedule "
"new alarms. The reason for using command line options for this purpose is "
"that if &kalarm; were started without any command line parameters and then "
"sent &DCOP; requests, it would start in its default graphical mode, which is "
"clearly undesirable for an inter-program request."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4184
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Programs should first check whether &kalarm; is already running; if it is, "
"they should instead use &DCOP; calls to request these operations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The command line options for scheduling a new alarm are as described in the "
"chapter <link linkend=\"cmdline-operation\">Command Line Operation</link>. "
"The options for triggering and canceling scheduled alarms are as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normal users may also if they wish use these command line options (assuming "
"that they can supply the necessary parameter information)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:4207
#, no-c-format
msgid "--cancelEvent <replaceable>eventID</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:4208
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cancel the alarm with the specified event ID."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:4211
#, no-c-format
msgid "--triggerEvent <replaceable>eventID</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:4212
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Trigger the alarm with the specified event ID. The action taken is the same "
"as for the <link linkend=\"triggerEvent\">triggerEvent()</link> &DCOP; call."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: option
#: index.docbook:4218
#, no-c-format
msgid "--handleEvent <replaceable>eventID</replaceable>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:4219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Trigger or cancel the alarm with the specified event ID. &kalarm; determines "
"which action to take in the same way as for the <link linkend=\"handleEvent"
"\">handleEvent()</link> &DCOP; call."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>--cancelEvent</option>, <option>--triggerEvent</option> and "
"<option>--handleEvent</option> are mutually exclusive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4231
#, no-c-format
msgid "Examples are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:4233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kalarm</command> <option>--"
"triggerEvent <replaceable>&kalarm;-387486299.702</replaceable></option></"
"userinput>\n"
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kalarm</command> <option>--"
"cancelEvent <replaceable>&kalarm;-388886299.793</replaceable></option></"
"userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:4241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Questions and Answers"
msgstr "Questions e responsas"

#. Tag: chapter
#: index.docbook:4241
#, no-c-format
msgid "&reporting.bugs; &updating.documentation;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4249
#, no-c-format
msgid "What is the alarm daemon?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <application>alarm daemon</application> is an application which runs in "
"the background, monitoring alarms and telling &kalarm; to trigger them when "
"they become due."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4260
#, no-c-format
msgid "What configuration files does &kalarm; use?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/config/kalarmrc</filename> holds your &kalarm; "
"preferences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4265
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/config/kalarmdrc</filename> holds preferences used "
"by the <application>alarm daemon</application>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/config/kresources/alarms/stdrc</filename> holds "
"your alarm resource configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Where does &kalarm; store its alarms?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The names of the calendar files which &kalarm; creates the first time it is "
"run are as follows (but these may be overridden by entries in the "
"<parameter>General</parameter> section of &kalarm;'s preferences file):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/kalarm/calendar.ics</filename> holds active "
"alarms (overridable by the <parameter>Calendar</parameter> entry)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/kalarm/expired.ics</filename> holds archived "
"alarms (overridable by the <parameter>ExpiredCalendar</parameter> entry)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4298
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/kalarm/template.ics</filename> holds alarm "
"templates (overridable by the <parameter>TemplateCalendar</parameter> entry)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4304
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can find out which calendar files are currently in use by viewing each "
"resource's details in the alarm resources list. The file names are stored in "
"the alarm resource configuration file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Details of alarms currently being displayed are stored in the calendar file "
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/kalarm/displaying.ics</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4316
#, no-c-format
msgid "What format are alarms stored in?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4319
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The calendar files in which &kalarm; stores its alarms are text files whose "
"format is defined by the document <ulink url=\"http://www.w3.org/2002/12/cal/"
"rfc2445.html\">RFC2445 - Internet Calendaring and Scheduling Core Object "
"Specification (iCalendar)</ulink>. This is the standard format used by all "
"kdepim applications. &kalarm; uses certain non-standard properties, in "
"conformance with RFC2445. In the VEVENT component: <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-"
"FLAGS</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-NEXTRECUR</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-"
"KALARM-REPEAT</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-ARCHIVE</literal>, <literal>X-"
"KDE-KALARM-LOG</literal>, and in the VALARM component: <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-"
"TYPE</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-NEXTREPEAT</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-"
"KALARM-FONTCOLOR</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-VOLUME</literal>, "
"<literal>X-KDE-KALARM-SPEAK</literal>, <literal>X-KDE-KALARM-KMAILID</"
"literal>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4342
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What are the application names of &kalarm; and the <application>alarm "
"daemon</application>?"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:4346
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kalarm;'s application name is <application>kalarm</application>, and the "
"<application>alarm daemon</application>'s application name is "
"<application>kalarmd</application>."
msgstr ""

